		<author><name><![CDATA[SA0BUX]]></name></author>
		<updated>2025-06-08T06:51:25</updated>

		<published>2025-06-08T06:51:25</published>
		<id>http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5156&amp;p=37412#p37412</id>
		<link href="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5156&amp;p=37412#p37412"/>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: NEW TYT MD9600 PLUS - 1750Hz Tone is quiet - DMR Display ?]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5156&amp;p=37412#p37412"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>Hello,<br><br>The frequency counter shows 1740 Hz, which is 10 Hz too low.<br><br>But I think the sound isn't modulated enough, which is why the repeaters can't be opened. It's noticeable that this only affects brand-new devices with V5 firmware!<br><br>73 Alfred OE7ABH</div></blockquote>I made a quick test on my newly arrived V5 radio which is still running factory firmware ( S126.061 ) by connecting demodulated output from <br>my Marconi TF2304 deviation meter to a frequency counter.<br>( Have never tried that before so I hope it's the right way to do it )   <br><br>The tone was 1751 Hz and and I also noticed that the deviation was 2 kHz for a NFM channel and 4 kHz for FM, so it seems fine with factory<br>firmware.<br>I also compared with my V2 radio running latest OpenGD77 and 1750 Hz was within a Hz or so but the deviation was lower, NFM 1.5 kHz &amp; 2 kHz on FM, the deviation on speech is lower than expected. <br><br>I will redo the tests when I moved over to OpenGD77 on the V5 radio.</div></blockquote>Radio is now upgraded to OpenGD77 20250323 V5<br><br>1750 Hz is almost spot on on the counter , tone deviation is lower than factory firmware: NFM 1.5 kHz &amp; FM 2 kHz which is similar to my V2<br>but speech deviation is wider than my V2 and similar to the V5 factory firmware ( around 2.5 kHZ NFM and 4 kHz FM )<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2867">SA0BUX</a> — Sun Jun 08, 2025 6:51 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
